      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalists heavily employ original public meaning, scrutinizing colonial-era common law and founding-era state militia documents to define the operative scope of \"arms.\" Their methodology seeks fixed meaning found in contemporaneous understanding, resisting legislative or social shifts. Living constitutionalists, however, frequently utilize evolving standards of \"reasonableness\" or reference the evolving nature of fundamental rights recognized throughout jurisprudence. They argue that the Constitution is a dynamic document meant to mediate modern human experiences, allowing core principles to remain valid even if their specific applications change.",
      "source": "target",
